    "kind": "free",
    "finalReminder": "A boundary is a clear statement of what you can offer, what you cannot accept, and how you will respond when a limit is crossed. It works best when it is specific, respectful, and consistent. Other people may feel disappointed, but disappointment alone does not prove you have acted wrongly. Protect your time and privacy without using limits to punish or control. Healthy relationships make room for honest needs on both sides."
