        "What does 'enough' mean for one area of your life right now?\n\nIf the situation involves another person, focus on observable behaviour and a clear request rather than a judgement about their character. If it is a personal habit, reduce the first step until it feels manageable. Either way, record what helped and what got in the way. Small adjustments are often more useful than a dramatic promise that is difficult to maintain.\n\nFinal reminder for this chapter: do not wait for perfect confidence before taking a reasonable step. Start carefully, learn from the result, and adjust where needed."
